course: dictionary
lesson: 7988
title: Fun words and careful words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Recreational is a formal word. It means done for fun, relaxing and enjoyment in your free time, not for work. «Recreational sport» is a game you play because you enjoy it.
explain: Use the words around it to work it out. Recreational comes from recreation, which means play and rest. Then test your meaning: «The town built a new recreational area by the river» makes sense if recreational means for fun and play.
explain: Some words are chosen to sound softer. Officials say «substance misuse» instead of addiction, and «recreational drugs» instead of illegal drugs. The careful word does not change what is true; it only changes how it sounds. Check a dictionary or ask a trusted adult when you are unsure.
fact: Recreational means done for fun, relaxing and enjoyment in your free time.
fact: Recreational is a formal word; in everyday talk you could say «for fun».
fact: A recreational area is a place for play and fun, like a park.
fact: «Recreational drugs» means illegal drugs taken for pleasure, not as medicine. They are still often illegal and harmful.
fact: Officials sometimes use cool, careful words: «substance misuse» instead of addiction, and «recreational drugs» instead of illegal drugs.
exercise: «They spent Saturday at the recreational centre, swimming and playing games.» What does recreational mean here? | Very dangerous | *Done for fun and play | Done for money at work | Closed for repairs
exercise: «The council wants to turn the old car park into a recreational area.» What is a recreational area most like? | A hospital ward | A busy road | *A park for play and fun | A shop selling tools
exercise: Officials say «substance misuse» instead of addiction. Why might they choose the careful words? | To show that the problem is happy | *To sound softer and less harsh | To make the meaning more exact in every way | Because the words are longer
test: Which word means the same as «for fun» in formal writing? | Necessary | *Recreational | Hurried | Compulsory
test: «Recreational drugs» means what? | Medicine given by a doctor | Drinks sold at a shop | *Illegal drugs taken for pleasure | Vitamins for children
exam: Officials say «recreational drugs» instead of illegal drugs. What does this careful choice show? | It means the drugs are only for children | It is the same as calling them medicine | *It is a softer word, but the drugs are still illegal and harmful | It means the drugs are safe to take
